<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Murong Nuohebo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 688</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murong-xianbei">Murong</a> Nuohebo was the last ruler of Tuyuhun, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianbei">Xianbei</a> kingdom around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qinghai-lake">Qinghai Lake</a>, reigning as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang dynasty</a> and married to a Tang princess. When the Tibetan Empire conquered Tuyuhun in 663 he fled with his followers into Tang territory. The Tang defeat at the Dafei River in 670 ended attempts to restore him, and his people were resettled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p></div>
